el of c-FLIP versus Fas determines susceptibility to Fas ligand-induced cell death in murine thymoma EL-4 cells</article-title><source>Exp Cell Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>273</volume><fpage>256</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11822881</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/excr.2001.5438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Irmler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thome</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hahne</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hofmann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Steiner</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Bodmer</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Schr&#x000f6;ter</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Burns</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattmann</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rimoldi</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>French</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>Tschopp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of death receptor signals by cellular FLIP</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1997</year><volume>388</volume><fpage>190</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9217161</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/40657</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>McLaughlin</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>McEwan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakai</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Redmond</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnston</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Longley</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>c-FLIP: A Key Regulator of Colorectal Cancer Cell Death</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>5754</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17575142</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-06-3585</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wajant</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Targeting the FLICE Inhibitory Protein (FLIP) in cancer therapy</article-title><source>Mol Interv</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>124</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14993418</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1124/mi.3.3.124</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Korkolopoulou</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Saetta</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Levidou</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gigelou</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Lazaris</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Thymara</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Scliri</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bousboukea</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Michalopoulos</surname><given-names>NV</given-names></name><name><surname>Apostolikas</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Konstantinidou</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tzivras</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Patsouris</surname><given-